{
    "background_story": "Drew's life took a dramatic turn when he providentially stumbled upon a small, quirky bookstore while lost in the city. The store's owner, an elderly man named George, took a liking to Drew and offered him a job on the spot. As Drew worked among the dusty shelves, he discovered a passion for writing and a talent for storytelling. George, sensing Drew's potential, became his mentor, guiding him through the world of literature. Under George's tutelage, Drew's writing flourished, and he soon landed a publishing deal. Years later, Drew's bestselling novel was adapted into a film, and he returned to the bookstore to thank George, who had providentially set him on the path to success. Drew never forgot the chance encounter that changed his life, and he made sure to pay it forward, helping aspiring writers in his community.",
